# keep decision records dir
## Decision Records Storage (`data/decision_records/.gitkeep`)

The `data/decision_records/` directory serves as the audit logging repository for all systematic alpha allocations, human-in-the-loop (HITL) sign-offs, pre-trade compliance checks, and emergency override actions.

---

### Directory Purpose & Compliance Scope

* **`Rebalance Decision Logs`**: Records point-in-time alpha factor rankings, target weight derivations, buffer band suppression logs, and lot rounding calculations.
* **`Signatory Audit Trail`**: Persists cryptographic signature hashes, timestamps, role authorizations, and approval notes from CCO and PM sign-offs.
* **`Pre-Trade Compliance Snapshots`**: Archives compliance audit reports for IRC Subchapter M (5/50 rule), SEC Rule 18f-4 (VaR), and SEC Rule 35d-1 (Names Rule).
* **`Regulatory Compliance (SEC Books & Records)`**: Supports immutable recordkeeping under SEC Rule 204-2 / Investment Company Act Rule 31a-1 (7-year retention).
* **`Version Control`**: The `.gitkeep` placeholder ensures the directory structure is maintained in source control while local execution artifacts (*.json, *.parquet, *.log) are excluded via `.gitignore`.
# data/decision_records/.gitkeep
# This placeholder file ensures the decision records directory is tracked by Git.
# Actual decision logs and signature hashes (*.json, *.parquet) should remain untracked via .gitignore.
